    <sys:String x:Key="L_YtZapretTitle">YouTube will not download?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_YtZapretBody">The built-in search uses yt-dlp. If your provider restricts YouTube (throttling, DPI), downloading may fail. BeatzOnKeys does not bundle any circumvention — that needs administrator rights. We recommend Zapret2UI. ⚠️ Circumvention tools are meant for research and educational use. Use them in accordance with the laws of your country.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_ZapretOpen">Open Zapret2UI</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecYouTube">YouTube</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeSearchT">Search and download</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeSearchX">The YouTube tab in the window title. Type a name and press Search for up to 10 results, with a small piano scene playing in the empty area while it works. The Add button next to a result keeps the track in your saved list. Paste a video link and the button beside the field becomes Download and fetches it directly, without searching. The background cache waits at most a minute per row: a slow one is marked Deferred and retried once at the end. A search preview plays in full: idle pausing does not apply to it. Downloaded tracks keep the pause.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeDownloadT">Links and limits</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeDownloadX">The Add button on a result row becomes active only once the track is cached, and then moves it into the downloaded list. Before that there is nothing to press: the file does not exist yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeCacheT">Cache and folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeCacheX">The cache switch decides whether played files stay on disk. Kept tracks counts only added tracks, search cache only the previews. Next to it are both clear buttons and the folder button. The cache always lives in the program data folder: &lt;Root&gt;\Music.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeYtDlpT">yt-dlp</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeYtDlpX">Downloads go through yt-dlp.exe. It is not fetched at startup: 22.5 MB arrive on the first action, with a progress bar. Download/Update yt-dlp repeats the download when it fails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeLimitsT">Failures and fallbacks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_YouTubeLimitsX">When access is refused (403/429, a bot check) the app tries Invidious mirrors and then reports that YouTube restricted access. If Windows cannot open M4A (N editions without Media Foundation), the audio is converted to WAV through ffmpeg.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecTikTok">TikTok</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLinkT">Paste a link, get the audio</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLinkX">Open TikTok, copy the link to a clip, paste it into the field and press Download. The program extracts the audio track and puts the file in Music\TikTok. There is no search by words here: TikTok does not hand out a list for a query without an account.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLinkShortT">Short links</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLinkShortX">A short vm.tiktok.com/… or vt.tiktok.com/… link works too: the program follows it first to learn the real address of the clip and only then fetches the audio. Pasting the same link again does not add a second copy of the track.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokCacheT">Its own cache and its own list</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokCacheX">TikTok files sit apart from the YouTube cache, and Clear TikTok cache removes only those. The downloaded-from-TikTok list is its own collection, separate from the Local playlist: counters and clearing are never shared.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLimitsT">What may not work</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TikTokLimitsX">If a clip is private, deleted or requires signing in, the program says so in plain words and adds nothing to the list. No cookies, tokens or sign-in are used: only what TikTok serves openly. If TikTok itself does not serve the clip to your connection, the last attempt asks the third-party service tikwm.com, so the clip link leaves for that service; it returns a direct address of the track and the file is downloaded from TikTok's own servers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_WindowTitle">BeatzOnKeys guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Guide">Guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecQuick">Quick start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q1T">1. Add MP3 or WAV files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q1X">Drop files onto the top card or press Add files. Only existing .mp3 and PCM .wav files are accepted, and the same file is not added twice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q2T">2. Pick a track</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q2X">Click a row in the Tracks list. The selected track and its duration appear in the card on the right.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q3T">3. Set the levels</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q3X">The volume sliders and the idle timeout are described below. Changes are saved automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q4T">4. Press Start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q4X">The track starts at 0:00 at the quiet level, the window stays open, and keyboard capture is installed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q5T">5. Type in any application</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q5X">An ordinary key raises the volume over 50 ms; after 150 ms without input it falls back over 200 ms.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q6T">6. Hide the window to the tray</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_Q6X">The close button does not quit: it hides the window while music and typing reactivity keep running.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecControls">Buttons and controls</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StartT">Start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StartX">Plays the selected track from the beginning at the quiet level and installs the keyboard hook. The window stays open. After Stop, the next Start begins at 0:00 again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PauseResumeT">Pause / Resume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PauseResumeX">The button appears while music is playing. Pause silences the output but remembers the spot: Resume returns to the exact same second of the track instead of starting over. Typing does not lift a pause — that is your explicit decision. When the track stopped on its own after the idle timeout, the button also offers Resume and returns it to the same second, but quietly: the first keystroke raises the volume.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StopT">Stop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StopX">Stops the music and removes the keyboard hook. An idle pause is not a stop: it keeps the position of the current run.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ResetT">Reset</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ResetX">Returns the playlist and the playback settings to their defaults: volumes, idle timeout, pause on idle, auto-advance, and loop. Language, theme, and the audio files stay as they are.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_DragT">Dragging a track</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_DragX">Hold the left button on a row and pull: a line shows where the track will land. The upper half of a row inserts before it, the lower half after it, and the empty space below the list means the end. The playing track is not restarted.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MoveT">Move up and down</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MoveX">The arrows in a track row change the order. The first row cannot move up and the last cannot move down; auto-advance follows the new order, and a reorder never interrupts the playing track.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ClearT">Clear all</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ClearX">Removes every track from the list, stops the music, and saves the empty playlist. The files on disk stay untouched.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AddT">Add files and drag and drop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AddX">Opens the file picker or accepts a drop. The top card is the drop area.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_RemoveT">Remove a track</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_RemoveX">The bin icon on a row removes the entry from the list; the file on disk stays.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_GuideT">Guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_GuideX">Opens this screen. It is also available with F1 and from the notification-area menu.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LogsT">Logs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LogsX">Opens the folder with daily UTF-8 journals, which help when something misbehaves.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AboutT">About</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AboutX">Shows the version, the author, links, and the update controls.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LangT">EN | RU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LangX">Switches the interface language immediately and remembers the choice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ThemeT">Sun and moon</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ThemeX">Switches the light and dark theme. The choice is saved.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_WinT">Window buttons</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_WinX">Minimize, maximize or restore (double-click the title bar), and hide to the tray. The close button never quits the app.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecSliders">Sliders and levels</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MaxT">Maximum volume: 0–100%</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MaxX">The level typing raises the volume to. Defaults to 100%. It is the ceiling: the quiet level can never exceed it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MinT">Minimum volume: 0–50%</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MinX">The quiet level while you are not typing. Defaults to 20%. The lower of the minimum and the maximum applies.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_IdleT">Idle timeout: 1–10 s</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_IdleX">How many seconds without input to wait before pausing, when Pause on idle is on. Defaults to 3 s.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ProgT">Position bar</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ProgX">Shows the position and duration of the selected track. It only reports: the app has no seeking.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SysVolT">Important: the Windows volume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SysVolX">The app multiplies its own level by the system volume. At 6% system level even 100% in the app is practically silent, so check the volume and the mute state.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecSwitches">Switches</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PauseT">Pause on idle</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PauseX">On by default. After the timeout the track pauses; the first key resumes at the same position and immediately at the maximum level.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AutoT">Advance to the next track</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AutoX">At the end of a track, continue with the next available one. Without it the track stays at its end.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LoopT">Loop playback</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_LoopX">Repeats the current track. Together with auto-advance the whole list repeats.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MatrixT">Behaviour at the end of a track</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_MatrixX">Advance off + loop off: stays at the end. Advance off + loop on: repeats the current track. Advance on + loop off: next track, stop after the last. Advance on + loop on: next track, and the list wraps to its start.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecReaction">Music reaction</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PunchT">Punch response</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PunchX">When the track just hit a transient (drums, kick), a key press reaches full volume in 15 ms instead of 50 ms, so the volume flashes follow the rhythm.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_BassT">Bass boost</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_BassX">While bass and kick (40–120 Hz) play, up to 30% is added to the gain. It never rises above the maximum volume, and 0% turns the effect off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StereoPulseT">Stereo pulse</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StereoPulseX">Shifts the balance left or right for 50 ms on each key press, alternating sides.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AdaptiveT">Adaptive threshold</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_AdaptiveX">A quiet track (RMS below 0.1) gets a 10% quiet level, a loud one (above 0.5) 30%, and an average track keeps your minimum volume.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecPanel">The Settings tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ChipsT">The Volume / Reaction / Behaviour chips</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_ChipsX">Three buttons above the settings. Pressing one opens that section and closes the others, so the panel always fits without scrolling. The active chip is tinted blue.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_CollapseT">Collapsing a section</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_CollapseX">Click a section header to fold it into one line. The ⌄ arrow means expanded and › means collapsed. You can still open several headers at once when you want to compare settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_CountT">The numbered circle</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_CountX">Appears on a collapsed section and tells how many settings it holds: 4 in Volume, 4 in Reaction, 2 in Behaviour. It shows at a glance that the section is not empty.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SummaryT">The summary beside the header</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SummaryX">A collapsed section shows its current values: "100% · 20% · 3 s", "bass 15% · stereo off". It updates the moment you move a slider, so the state reads without expanding.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecTray">Notification area (tray)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayIconT">The tray icon</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayIconX">Double-click the icon to bring the window back. The icon exists while the app runs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayMenuT">The icon menu</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayMenuX">Open BeatzOnKeys, Guide, About, Stop playback, and Exit. Exit really quits the app.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayLaunchT">Launching again</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_TrayLaunchX">When the app already runs, a second launch restores its window instead of starting another copy.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecStatus">Status line</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StatusT">The line at the bottom</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_StatusX">Ready means you can start. Playing means the track runs and typing raises the volume. Idle paused means press any key. Track ended means enable loop or press Stop, then Start. The current track and position appear below it.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecKeys">Keyboard</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_KeysT">Which keys count as typing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_KeysX">Shift, Ctrl, and Alt alone are ignored, as are CapsLock and the Windows keys. Every other key, including Enter, the arrows, and Backspace, raises the volume.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecPrivacy">Privacy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PrivacyT">What the hook sees</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PrivacyX">Only that a key was pressed. Characters, the clipboard, window titles, and application names are never read or recorded. The hook runs only after Start.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecTrouble">If something does not work</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_NoSoundT">No sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_NoSoundX">Check that the track is available, an output device is selected, the Windows volume is up, and nothing is muted. While idle the app deliberately plays quietly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_QuietT">Too quiet while idle</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_QuietX">Raise the minimum volume, remembering that it cannot exceed the maximum.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PausesT">Unexpected pauses</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_PausesX">That is the idle timeout: raise it or turn Pause on idle off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_HiddenT">The window disappeared</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_HiddenX">The close button hides the window to the tray. Double-click the tray icon, or launch BeatzOnKeys again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_EndT">The track stays at its end</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_EndX">Press Stop, then Start, or enable loop or auto-advance.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_UpdStorageT">The update will not download or will not install</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_UpdStorageX">The update downloads into the program data folder and swaps the file on the next start. If the transfer breaks, the bytes already on disk are kept and the next attempt continues from there. All data — settings, logs, cache, updates — lives under one root: beside the exe, in a folder you picked, or in %LOCALAPPDATA%\BeatzOnKeys. News and releases: t.me/beatzonkeys.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_NotSavedT">Settings are not saved</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_NotSavedX">When the profile folder is not writable the app says so at startup. Settings live in the user profile.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_SecFiles">Where the data lives</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_FilesT">Paths</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Guide_FilesX">Everything lives under one root, {0}: settings.json holds the preferences, library.json the track collection, Logs\ the daily journals, Music\ the YouTube cache, Music\TikTok\ what came from TikTok, and updates\ the staged updates. The program folder only needs BeatzOnKeys.exe.</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
